      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pineapple base: 12 dc into a ch-4 space. Row 2: ch 3, tr in each dc, ch 3, tr. Row 3 onward: dc at start and end, ch 2, (tr, ch 1) across reducing by 1 cluster per row. Final row: dc in the single remaining ch-sp. The pineapple repeats every 14 sts. Place a tr column (1 tr) between each panel and at each edge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 50. Row 1: establish 3 pineapple bases of 12 dc separated by tr columns. Turn."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
